Ask the font server several things at once, when nothing waits for the
answers in between.

With the font on a server over the internet, each ask is a round trip, and
the editor used to make them one after another: the font controller's
initialize() asked 8 things in a row, and the shaper controller asked for
the features, the conditional substitutions and the kerning only after the
backend's shaper font, one by one. At 70 ms a round trip, that is about
0.7 s of waiting before a glyph shows. Now initialize() asks them together,
and the shaper controller asks for its data early, together with the shaper
font; FontController.getData gives everyone who asks meanwhile the answer
of the one request on its way.

What Fontra does is the same; only the order of the asks changes.

